<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The update feed for Maven Babelfish, with nothing in it yet.

  Publish this file at https://ghost-labs.com/babelfish/appcast.xml BEFORE the first release, not
  after. Three reasons, and the first is the one that matters:

  1. That address is compiled into every copy of the application and can never change, because an
     install only knows the address it was built with. Proving it is live and served over https
     while nothing depends on it is free; finding out it is wrong after a package is in somebody
     else's hands is not.
  2. An empty feed is a complete answer. Sparkle reads it, finds nothing newer than what is running,
     and says nothing — which is correct. A 404 is an error on every daily check of every install.
  3. publish.sh merges each release into whatever is already published, and falls back to writing a
     fresh feed only when there is none. Publishing this first means the first real release takes
     the merge path, which is the one every release after it will take too.

  Do not hand-edit this once it is live. publish.sh appends each new entry after the language line
  and keeps the old ones, so an install two versions behind still finds a path forward.
-->
<rss version="2.0" xmlns:sparkle="http://www.andymatuschak.org/xml-namespaces/sparkle">
    <channel>
        <title>Maven Babelfish</title>
        <link>https://ghost-labs.com/babelfish/appcast.xml</link>
        <description>Updates to Maven Babelfish.</description>
        <language>en</language>
    </channel>
</rss>
